# Contribution workflow

- Treat the checked-in source as the canonical implementation.
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, customer exports, screenshots of customer data, or production database dumps.
- Use environment variables for deployment-specific URLs and secrets.
- Keep business records and contact details out of test fixtures; use synthetic data and reserved example domains.
- Run the relevant checks before proposing a change and describe any unverified integration clearly.
- Do not claim a third-party integration is live unless its authorization and end-to-end behavior have been tested.
